<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Buxentum</span></b> , i, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυξοῦς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Lucania</i>, <i>of
				Greek origin</i>, <i>colonized by the Romans after
				the second Punic war</i>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
				15, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 34, 45, 2</span></i>; now <i>Policastro</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				23, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Buxentīnus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of Buxentum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Colon. p. 90</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Buxen-tĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pubes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 585</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
